                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 389</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The issue of the bilateral United States-Spanish talks on bases in Spain and the
                    possibility of future United States sponsorship of Spain in NATO were briefly
                    discussed at the Fifth Meeting of the Foreign Ministers of the United States,
                    the United Kingdom, and France at Washington on September 13, 1951. For the
                    record of this meeting, see <ref target="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg_1279">volume III,
                        Part 1, page 1279</ref>.</p>
            </div>
